{
  "title": "Merits of Reciting Ayat al-Kursi after Every Namaz",
  "data": "Through a valid chain of authority, Imam Musa ibn Ja'far (a) is reported to have said, \"Whoever recites [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) after every prayer will not be afflicted by stings of stingers.\"\nAccording to another validly reported tradition, Imam al-Kazim (a) is reported to have quoted the Holy Prophet (s) as saying to Imam Ali (a), \"O Ali! Keep on reciting [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) after every obligatory prayer, because not everyone keeps on reciting it save a prophet, a veracious person, or a martyr.\"\nThe Holy Prophet (s) is reported to have said, \"Whoever recites [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) after every prayer, nothing will prevent him from entering Paradise except death.\"\nAccording to another tradition, \"Whoever recites [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) after obligatory prayers will have his prayers accepted, will be in the security of Allah, and will be saved by Almighty Allah from misfortunes and sinning.\""
}
